# Database & Prisma Rules

Source of truth: `docs/platform/02_DATABASE_SCHEMA.md`. Keep `schema.prisma` and that document in sync in the same change.

## Schema conventions
- Models `PascalCase` with `@@map("snake_case_plural")`; columns `@map("snake_case")`.
- PK: `String @id @default(dbgenerated("gen_random_uuid()")) @db.Uuid`.
- Business tables carry `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, and `deletedAt` (soft delete) — all `@db.Timestamptz`.
- Money: `Decimal @db.Decimal(14,2)`. Coordinates: `Decimal @db.Decimal(9,6)`. Dates without time: `@db.Date`.
- Enums over free-text status columns; new enum values are appended (never renamed) once deployed.
- Every foreign key gets an `@@index`; composite indexes follow the query's filter order.
- Business reference numbers (`refNo`, `trackingNo`, …) are `@unique` and generated by the Sequence engine, never by clients.

## Migrations
- Create with `npm run prisma:migrate -- --name <verb>_<object>`; commit the generated SQL; never edit an applied migration.
- Destructive changes (drop column/table, type narrowing) require approval and an expand → backfill → contract plan across releases.
- Views, trigram/GIN indexes, partitions, and `REVOKE` grants on `audit_logs` live in hand-written SQL migrations.
- CI runs `prisma validate`, `prisma migrate diff` (drift check), and `prisma migrate deploy` on a fresh database.

## Seed
- `prisma/seed.ts` is idempotent (`upsert` by natural keys); persona passwords come from env, never literals.
- Seed data mirrors the prototype's realistic sample set (doc 02 §6) so demos match.

## Never
- Never run `prisma migrate reset`, `db push --force-reset`, or `DROP` statements against shared/prod databases without explicit approval.
